# `fluid::Sense`

Whether a state control fires below or above its threshold.

## Signature

```cpp
fluid::Sense
```

## What It Does

Gives the direction of a `StateControl`. `Below` fires when the watched value is below the threshold and `Above` when it is above it.

## Fields

| Field | Meaning | Default |
|---|---|---|
| `Below` | Fires when the level or pressure head falls below the threshold. |  |
| `Above` | Fires when it rises above the threshold. |  |

## Returns

An enumeration; `StateControl::sense`.

## Errors

None.

## Interpretation and Use

Pair an `Above` rule with a `Below` rule at different thresholds to make a hysteresis band: the thresholds the wrong way round make rules that cannot settle.

